From a83a55c99c68c9edaea64f84a544f4cb80c595e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:04:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: writes outside the texels in use leave cached pages
 alone (level video screens); STR pictures decoded on four cores with a
 transform that skips zeros

- t31's dips (15-17 fps, ~6 pages freed and ~6 updated a frame): no palette writes in a level,
  and the same-bytes skip stays 0 because the bytes do change: the writes are the song's 96-wide
  video going to a level's screen (PC_VdecToTexture), ~100 rows ~15 times a second into a page
  other textures share. Every cached page on that VRAM page (each CLUT) was redone per picture.
- Each slot keeps the box of texels its faces have used (SlotUse, from GlVert.uvr; a texture
  window: all). A write outside the box leaves the slot alone; its rows are decoded when a
  face first reaches them, and CacheCheck skips them till then (THPS_GL_USEDBOX=0: as t31).
  Updates in place have no row limit now and use the decode threads from 32 rows. No GPU wait
  in them. [gl] line: writes outside the texels in use.
- FMV: STR pictures took ~70 ms each on the game's core (14 fps): a full 1024-multiply transform
  per block. VideoDecoder::Block skips zero rows and coefficients (a DC-only block is one value),
  Clamp8 no longer calls lrintf, and Frame decodes columns of macroblocks on the game thread and
  3 threads on cores 1-3 (a first walk through the codes finds where each share starts;
  THPS_FMV_THREAD=0: the game thread alone). Boot of a movie logs "[fmv] ...". The levels' video
  screens use the same decoder. Off-device, a synthetic 320x240 frame: 15-bit identical, 24-bit
  1 byte of 230400 off by 1 (rounding), split by shares identical to whole.
---
 platform/pc/README.md           |   2 +
 platform/pc/include/pc/gl_gpu.h |   9 ++
 platform/pc/include/pc/vdec.h   |  14 ++-
 platform/pc/src/pc_gpu_gl.cpp   |  90 +++++++++++----
 platform/pc/src/pc_vdec.cpp     | 195 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 5 files changed, 255 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platform/pc/README.md b/platform/pc/README.md
index 0bbb987..1986348 100644
--- a/platform/pc/README.md
+++ b/platform/pc/README.md
@@ -579,6 +579,8 @@ window, `THPS_FAST`, `THPS_DETERMINISTIC`) never wait for a display.
 | `THPS_GL_SAMEBYTES=0` | texture writes of the bytes already there are done anyway (default t31: skipped) |
 | `THPS_GL_PRECISEINV=0` | a texture write reaches the cached pages by 16x16 cells at the next draw (default t31: its exact rectangle) |
 | `THPS_GL_PARTIAL=0` | cached pages a write reaches are freed (default t31: pages drawn lately have the written rows decoded again in place) |
+| `THPS_GL_USEDBOX=0` | a texture write reaches a cached page wherever it lands on it (default t32: only if a face has used those texels) |
+| `THPS_FMV_THREAD=0` | Vita: STR movie pictures and video screens decoded by the game thread alone (default t32: with 3 threads on cores 1-3) |
 | `THPS_FILE_DIRECT=0` | Vita: game files read with stdio as before t28 (default: sceIoRead in pieces of 1 MB, an open reads only the header) |
 | `THPS_GL_DECODE_THREADS=n` | Vita: texture cache pages decoded by n threads on cores 1-3 with the game thread (default 3, 0 = the game thread alone) |
 | `THPS_GL_NODISCARD=0` | OpenGL ES (Vita), batched 3D: no separate no-discard, no-blend program for opaque faces with no transparent texel under them |
